1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,933
Studying alone is hard.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,967
Cram Club makes starting easier.

3
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:08,433
Make your character, so you can show up
next to people without a webcam.

4
00:00:08,767 --> 00:00:10,433
A quick camera and mic check first.

5
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,767
The camera's optional,
and video never leaves your computer.

6
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:16,300
Then walk into the Grand Reading Hall.

7
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:18,267
Everyone here is a real student.

8
00:00:18,567 --> 00:00:19,600
There's a library chat.

9
00:00:19,667 --> 00:00:21,700
If nobody answers you within ten seconds,

10
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:23,733
Ms. Fenwick, the librarian, steps in.

11
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,467
Nobody gets left on read.

12
00:00:25,967 --> 00:00:28,933
Sit at any table to hold it
for an hour, open or private.

13
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:32,100
Press P, and your desk clock
starts a pomodoro.

14
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:35,433
Judges can jump straight in at /demo.

15
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:38,367
Turn your camera on
and your character copies your face.

16
00:00:38,433 --> 00:00:41,733
Only eight numbers leave your laptop,
never video.

17
00:00:42,067 --> 00:00:46,233
Look away for eight seconds
and Ms. Fenwick shushes you, kindly, by name.

18
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:49,000
Ask her anything.
She researches it with TinyFish,

19
00:00:49,067 --> 00:00:50,333
credible sources first,

20
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,733
and answers with every source shown.

21
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,667
She turns it into a narrated
whiteboard lesson.

22
00:00:55,733 --> 00:00:57,067
There's a quiz question

23
00:00:57,133 --> 00:01:00,000
and you get a hint, then another try.

24
00:01:00,333 --> 00:01:04,433
Or open the Learning Studio book
to turn your own notes into a lesson.

25
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:08,633
Finish a pomodoro and you get
real focus minutes and XP.

26
00:01:08,867 --> 00:01:11,367
Track your XP and streaks,
which forgive one bad day,

27
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:13,333
plus community charts.

28
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:16,700
And it's real: private Vultr storage
with signed links,

29
00:01:16,767 --> 00:01:18,967
Tiger Data records that check themselves,

30
00:01:19,033 --> 00:01:21,400
and single-use game tickets.

31
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:25,567
Cram Club. Start studying, next to someone.

